-- Migration 1918 — withdraw 228 stance chairs from the absence tier-B MIDDLE BAND (score 0.50-0.80).
--
-- WHAT THIS IS. The companion to migration 1918. The top band (score >= 0.80, 193 rows) was read
-- first and came in at 80.8%. This is the next band down, 367 rows, which the fresh blind control
-- had estimated at ~56%. All 367 are now adjudicated: 351 read in this pass plus the 16 already
-- read under the same standard in that control sample. **Result: 228/367 = 62.1%.**
--
-- 🔑 THE BANDS CAME OUT IN THE RIGHT ORDER AND THE RANKER IS WHAT PUT THEM THERE:
--   >= 0.80 → 80.8% (mig 1917) · 0.50-0.80 → 62.1% (here) · < 0.50 → 0 of 9 sampled.
-- The model was fitted on the 307 hand-read tier-A rows and never saw any of these.
--
-- ⚖ ADJUDICATED UNDER `C:/ev-stance-work/absence/STANDARD.md`, the written rule derived from the
-- tier-A ledger's own 101 KEEP rulings and validated at 92% agreement on 24 fresh blind rows.
-- 🔑 THE STANDARD IS DOING WORK, MEASURABLY: 13 of these rows had been read BEFORE it existed, by a
-- reader since measured as 50% drifted on KEEPs. Re-read under the standard, **4 of the 13 flipped
-- to KEEP** — rows that would otherwise have been blanked wrongly.
--
-- ⚖ WHAT A BLANK HERE ASSERTS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT. It asserts that the row's own reasoning does
-- not support the chair it carries. It does NOT assert the person holds no view. Each row records
-- WHICH KIND of nothing it is.
--
-- 🔑 WHY A SEASON 2 BLANK. Season 1 is closed. A Season 2 answer of 0 SUPPRESSES — `NULLIF(pa.value,
-- 0)`, the guard outside the season collapse. Same mechanism as migrations 1914-1917.
--
-- COMPOSITION. 228 rows across 173 people. 218 INSERT, 10 UPDATE.
--
-- THE SHAPES. 🔴 Two dominate, and they are different from the top band's:
--   **NONCOSP 53** — the evidence is a NON-ACT (did not co-sponsor a named bill, or a recorded
--   non-vote), overwhelmingly seating the status-quo middle rung.
--   **RUNGTEXT 53** — the seated rung's own wording does not describe the evidence; typically the
--   row's prose argues for a NEIGHBOURING rung and seats this one anyway. This shape is the middle
--   band's signature: the evidence is often real and on-axis, and the MAPPING is what fails.
--   Then AFFIRM 33 · OFFAXIS 26 · ADMITS 21 · AFFIL 11 · BODY 9 · AWAY 8 · DUTY 4 · SCORE 1.
--
-- ⚠ NOT BLANKED — 139 of the 367, a much larger share than the top band's 37 of 193, exactly as the
-- lower score predicted. The clearest keeps name an instrument whose CONTENT is the rung's own
-- distinguishing clause: Cardin's enacted act funding abortion care (the clause unique to chair 1),
-- Moulton's cosponsorship of a bill REPEALING an existing voucher credit, Rosenbarger's vote
-- eliminating parking minimums, Guillen's twelve Medicaid-expansion bills.
--
-- Applied by hand via psql; no migration runner exists in this repo, so "applied" means its data
-- effects are live. Guards below fail the whole transaction rather than write a partial result.

